# Sovereign Platform — trivy CVE allow-list.
#
# Trivy reads this file at scan time and skips the listed CVEs when
# computing exit status. Every entry MUST justify itself inline — an
# assessor reading this file is the audit trail for why these CVEs
# don't block a release.
#
# Lifecycle:
#   - Entries listed here are tracked as POA&M items in
#     docs/ssp/poam.md (cluster id 5.4-CVE-*).
#   - Each entry is reviewed quarterly against the upstream Debian /
#     Alpine security tracker; entries with an available fixed version
#     in the chassis base image MUST be removed (and the base bumped).
#   - Last review: 2026-05-24.

# ── OpenSSL (Debian bookworm libssl3) ────────────────────────────────
# All OpenSSL findings are in the system-shipped libssl3 / openssl
# packages. The chassis services use Python's `ssl` module backed by
# the OS OpenSSL, but every chassis-controlled TLS endpoint is
# terminated upstream by the agency LB (per docs/ssp/controls/sc.md
# SC-12); these CVEs are not directly reachable from the chassis HTTP
# surface. Bumping is gated on Debian point-release availability.
CVE-2025-15467   # openssl: oversized Initial packet (QUIC) — chassis does not speak QUIC
CVE-2025-69421   # openssl: PKCS#12 malformed file DoS — chassis does not parse PKCS#12
CVE-2026-28387   # openssl: DANE TLSA UAF — chassis does not use DANE/TLSA
CVE-2026-28388   # openssl: delta CRL NULL deref — chassis does not parse CRLs
CVE-2026-28389   # openssl: CMS processing DoS — chassis does not parse CMS
CVE-2026-28390   # openssl: CMS Envelope NULL deref — same
CVE-2026-31789   # openssl: X.509 heap overflow on 32-bit — chassis runs 64-bit

# ── libxml2 (portal nginx:alpine image) ──────────────────────────────
# CVE-2026-6732 (HIGH, CVSS 7.5) — libxml2 XSD-validation type-confusion
# DoS. Fixed in libxml2 2.13.9-r1. TIME-BOXED allow-list, NOT a
# permanent waiver: the fix IS published on aarch64 and the Dockerfile's
# `apk upgrade` already pulls it there, but the Alpine 3.21 x86_64
# backport is still propagating and libxml2 cannot be force-upgraded
# ahead of it (nginx-module-xslt/njs + libxslt hard-link libxml2.so.2).
# Reachability: the portal is a static nginx file server for the
# pre-built SPA — it does not parse XSD-validated XML, so the DoS path is
# not in its runtime call graph. POA&M 5.4-CVE-libxml2 tracks removal;
# this entry MUST be deleted the moment `apk add libxml2>=2.13.9-r1`
# resolves on x86_64 (re-check at next quarterly review).
CVE-2026-6732    # libxml2: XSD-validation DoS — fix pending x86_64 backport; portal serves static files only

# ── GnuTLS (Debian-shipped, not used by chassis) ─────────────────────
# Pulled in transitively by ca-certificates, apt, gnupg — none of the
# chassis Python services link gnutls or use it at runtime. Tracked
# for OS-level updates; service surface unaffected.
CVE-2025-32988   # gnutls: otherName SAN export double-free
CVE-2025-32990   # gnutls: certtool template parsing heap overflow
CVE-2026-33845   # gnutls: DTLS zero-length fragment DoS
CVE-2026-33846   # gnutls: DTLS handshake fragment heap overflow
CVE-2026-3833    # gnutls: nameConstraints case-sensitive policy bypass
CVE-2026-42009   # gnutls: DTLS packet reordering DoS
CVE-2026-42010   # gnutls: RSA-PSK auth bypass via NUL in username

# ── GnuPG / libcap / sqlite / xz / pam (system, not reachable) ───────
# Used by apt + pip during build only; not in the runtime call graph
# of any chassis service.
CVE-2025-68973   # GnuPG: armor_filter OOB write — build-time tool only
CVE-2026-4878    # libcap: TOCTOU in cap_set_file — chassis does not call cap_set_file
CVE-2025-6965    # sqlite: integer truncation — chassis does not use sqlite
CVE-2025-31115   # xz: heap UAF in threaded decoder — chassis does not decompress xz at runtime
CVE-2025-6020    # linux-pam: directory traversal — chassis does not authenticate via PAM

# ── Perl (build/install tooling only) ────────────────────────────────
# Perl is pulled in by debianutils + base-files but not invoked by any
# chassis service runtime.
CVE-2023-31484   # perl: CPAN.pm TLS verification — chassis does not run CPAN at runtime
CVE-2024-56406   # perl: heap buffer overflow — chassis does not invoke perl at runtime

# ── Python packaging metadata findings ───────────────────────────────
# setuptools/wheel CVEs are about malicious package installation. The
# chassis Dockerfile installs from pinned dependency declarations; no
# untrusted wheels are downloaded at runtime.
CVE-2024-6345    # pypa/setuptools: RCE via package_index download
CVE-2025-47273   # setuptools: PackageIndex path traversal
CVE-2026-24049   # wheel: privilege escalation via malicious wheel
